WEBVTT

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.976
And the last time the rich guy invited us,

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.136
he also invited a couple of philosophers.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.688
These guys were philosophers of mind.

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:09.076
Their specialty was the philosophy
of consciousness.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.790
And they were full of all kinds of jargon.

00:04:11.814 --> 00:04:14.210
I'm trying to remember the words --

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:18.124
"monism," "dualism,"
categories all over the place.

00:04:18.148 --> 00:04:21.722
I didn't know what those meant, neither
did Dick or Sydney, for that matter.

00:04:21.746 --> 00:04:23.516
And what did we talk about?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:26.115
Well, what do you talk about
when you talk about minds?

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:28.303
There's one obvious thing to talk about:

00:04:28.327 --> 00:04:29.976
Can a machine become a mind?